# Files where a change is a security decision, not a refactor.
#
# On 2026-08-20 a roles-rename cleanup (`7c9ee664`, 39 files, 720 deletions) merged over a security
# batch shipped hours earlier and removed seven controls — the forced-password-change guard,
# refresh-token reuse detection, login timing equalisation, socket-room entitlement, and more.
# Every one of them lived under a path listed below. Requiring a named reviewer here would have put
# a human in front of that diff.
#
# GitHub only enforces this when branch protection has "Require review from Code Owners" enabled on
# the branch. Without that setting this file is documentation, not a gate — turn it on for `main`
# and `test` in Settings → Branches.
#
# Replace @DeepStacker with a team handle once there is more than one reviewer; a CODEOWNERS entry
# naming only the author of most commits cannot function as a second pair of eyes.

